.Dd January 25, 2026
.Dt DEVICE 9
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm struct device
.Nd generic device abstraction structure
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In kern/device.h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Vt struct device
is the core data structure used to represent a hardware device within the kernel's device model. It provides a unified view of the system's hardware topology, resource allocation, and driver binding.
.Pp
All devices, regardless of the bus they reside on (PCI, USB, etc.), are represented by an instance of this structure.
.Sh FIELDS
.Bl -tag -width "power_state"
.It Vt uint32_t vendor_id
The hardware vendor identifier (e.g., PCI Vendor ID).
.It Vt uint32_t device_id
The hardware device identifier (e.g., PCI Device ID).
.It Vt uint16_t class
The base device class code.
.It Vt uint16_t subclass
The device subclass code.
.It Vt uint8_t progif
The programming interface code.
.It Vt char serial[32]
A string comprising the device's serial number, if available.
.It Vt uint8_t guid[16]
A globally unique identifier for the device (e.g., UUID/GUID).
.It Vt struct device *parent
Pointer to the parent device (e.g., the bus controller or bridge). NULL for the root device.
.It Vt struct device *children
Pointer to the first child device (head of the children list).
.It Vt struct device *sibling
Pointer to the next device in the parent's children list.
.It Vt struct resource *resources
List of resources (I/O ports, memory ranges, IRQs, DMA channels) assigned to this device.
.It Vt int power_state
Current power management state of the device (D0-D3).
.It Vt int ref_count
Reference count for the device object's lifecycle.
.It Vt struct driver *driver
Pointer to the device driver bound to this device. NULL if no driver is attached.
.It Vt struct bus_type *bus
Pointer to the bus type definition that manages this device.
.It Vt uint32_t flags
Status flags indicating device state (e.g., initialized, suspended).
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bus 9 ,
.Xr driver 9 ,
.Xr resource 9
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Vt struct device
interface first appeared in Substrate.
